Recommends: cloud-image-utils,
            openssh-client,
            wget
Suggests: ansible,
          dnsmasq-base,
          docker.io,
          iproute2
Description: CLI tool for running, generating and listing QEMU VMs
 qemu-tool provides four subcommands: run-vm launches a QEMU virtual machine
 with a flexible set of options for networking, storage, PCI passthrough, and
 architecture (amd64, arm64, riscv64); gen-vm creates a new cloud-init-seeded
 VM image using debootstrap or a cloud image download; compose wraps
 docker compose for the vfio-user GPU VM stacks; and list reports the QEMU VMs
 running on the node, identifying which of them qemu-tool started.
 .
 The package itself has no Python runtime dependencies, but the subcommands
 shell out to external tools. qemu-system-* and qemu-img (qemu-utils) are
 required. gen-vm additionally needs cloud-localds (cloud-image-utils), wget
 and ssh, and needs ansible only when --ansible-playbook is used. run-vm needs
 ip (iproute2) and dnsmasq only for its TAP/bridge networking modes. compose
 needs docker; list uses docker only to resolve container names and degrades
 gracefully without it.
 .
 VM images are stored in /var/lib/qemu-tool/images (kvm group writable).
